Neverball and Neverputt 1.6.0 (Robert Kooima and Neverball contributors).

Source: https://neverball.org/neverball-1.6.0.tar.gz
SHA256: 73fe63cca4f96e2d355480d03bc0b2904e83a0abdf65fe8c52db5cc3cca88fa0

Code: GPL version 2 or later; see LICENSE.md and license-GPL-2.0.txt.
Selected ball/, putt/ and share/ modules retain their upstream notices and
style. neverball.c and neverputt.c adapt the original main.c entry points
and retain GPL notices. The new native platform code uses the generated9
root LICENSE; the combined games remain GPL. Assets retain their original
licenses and are installed separately, including all upstream legal notices.

Local integration:
- One native 6c/mk build and common platform for both games. The former
  sys/src/games/neverputt tree now lives in sys/src/games/neverball.
- Libdraw/libevent window, mouse and keyboard input, TinyGL/VirGL rendering.
  Native keyboard character records handle Unicode player/replay names.
- System PNG/JPEG readers and libttf replace SDL image/font dependencies.
- Native PCM mixer with pause/resume; Ogg assets decoded by audio/oggdec.
- Native filesystem, key names, timing, environment and date handling.
- Explicit wire-endian SOL reads/writes, proper prototypes and opaque type
  signatures for the Plan 9 compiler; C stdio string streams own formatting.
- Triangle indices use arrays so element buffers contain no struct padding.
- mapc clamps rounded normal dot products before acos and reports missing
  texture images, retaining finite unit coordinates for default materials.
- Menus expose native window settings and supported rendering options.
  English, mouse and keyboard; no SDL, HMD, fullscreen, reflection or MSAA.
- Accepting Neverputt's final score with the keyboard returns to the title,
  matching the mouse path; standalone holes may omit background music.
- Neverball's camera fade uses a bounded ratio before cubing, including
  zero-duration fades without floating-point division by zero.
- Set cleanup accepts an uninitialized set list, including early exits.

Original data are installed by boot/getneverball with their complete legal
notices; boot/getneverputt remains an alias. mk data compiles all maps and
shared models in the guest. See README, neverball(1) and neverputt(1).
